# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exam content must never be committed. This repo is public.
#
# The app reads question banks, papers and templates from a folder the teacher
# chooses at runtime, which is normally a school OneDrive or Teams folder. None
# of that belongs here. These rules exist so that a stray copy, a test fixture
# or an accidental save into the repo directory cannot become a public
# disclosure of an unreleased exam.
#
# If you need a sample for development, write a fake one under src/fixtures/
# and keep it obviously fictional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

bank/
banks/
papers/
templates/
content/
sample_exams/

# Syllabus models, all of them, not just the IB ones.
#
# A syllabus is copyright. The NESA Stage 6 (2013) notice permits a NSW teacher
# to copy reasonable portions for bona fide study and forbids reproducing a major
# extract, modifying the material, or commercial use; IB subject-guide content is
# licensed through the Programme Resource Centre. A generated model is a complete
# content inventory, restructured, published worldwide. That is not a reasonable
# portion under anyone's reading.
#
# So Klunk ships the generator, never the output. Each teacher generates a model
# from their own copy into their own folder. If a syllabus ever arrives under a
# licence that clearly permits republication, this is the line to revisit, and
# the model's source.redistributable flag is the thing to check first.
syllabus/*.json

# Profiles are NOT excluded. A profile records the shape of a paper - 40 marks,
# three sections at 10/15/15, five minutes reading time - which is fact about a
# public examination, not NESA's expression of its syllabus. Shipping them is
# what makes Klunk useful on first run.

# Source and generated documents. A school exam template, a past paper or a
# built paper are all one of these.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.xlsx
*.odt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
dist/
dist-single/
*.local
.vite/

